Make search5/navidrome@feat-podcast-ux-improvements/5420 buildable and upgradable
(upstream PR navidrome/navidrome#5949, HEAD 07cf48cb).

Two independent defects, both reported at
https://github.com/navidrome/navidrome/pull/5949#issuecomment-5591324891

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
1. core/podcasts/podcasts.go -- the branch does not compile
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    core/podcasts/podcasts.go:8:2:    "net" imported and not used
    core/podcasts/podcasts.go:10:2:   "net/url" imported and not used
    core/podcasts/podcasts.go:315:12: undefined: validateURL
    core/podcasts/podcasts.go:539:12: undefined: validateURL

validateURL was never deleted -- it was never written. Four commits within 65
seconds on 2026-09-07, all through the GitHub web editor, add the pieces around
it and nothing else:

    cb193a0e8a  adds the "net" and "net/url" imports
    037fcfd8d7  adds the call in fetchAndParse
    a2aaf3e9d6  puts /podcast/preview behind adminOnlyMiddleware
    07cf48cb8c  adds the call in doDownload

That burst is a security hardening pass, so an SSRF guard was the intent -- which
is also why "net" is imported.

No reusable helper exists in the tree. conf.validateURL (conf/configuration.go:906)
is unexported with a different signature; the plugin host client's check is a method
on httpServiceImpl coupled to per-plugin permissions; core/artwork/agent_images.go:35
rolls its own inline. A local function is what the codebase convention calls for.

The reconstruction mirrors both precedents: scheme and host checks from
conf.validateURL, address check from isPrivateOrLoopback in plugins/host_httpclient.go.
Like that one it inspects IP literals only, so it does not stop DNS rebinding.

KNOWN: this leaves the branch's own suite at 78 passed / 23 failed. Every failure
is this guard rejecting httptest fixtures on 127.0.0.1. A scheme-only variant
passes 101/101 but implements no SSRF protection; the guard was kept because the
pod's CiliumNetworkPolicy permits egress to `world`, which includes the home LAN.
Neither the Docker build nor pre-commit runs those tests.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. db/db.go -- existing installations cannot upgrade
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The five podcast migrations carry April 2026 timestamps, but the branch is rebased
on master, whose schema is already well past them. goose refuses migrations that
sort before the current version, so any existing database fails at startup:

    Failed to apply new migrations
    error: found 5 missing migrations before current version 20260703013908

Verified locally as a controlled experiment: an unpatched binary against a database
at that version reproduces the fatal error exactly; with goose.WithAllowMissing()
all five apply, the eight podcast_* tables are created, the versions are recorded,
and pre-existing tables are untouched.

Passing WithAllowMissing is the minimal fix for a test instance. Upstream should
renumber the migrations instead -- the flag relaxes ordering for every migration,
not just these. It is safe here only because the five are self-contained: they
create and alter podcast_* tables they own and touch nothing else.

